{title: 493 - Fill My Cup, Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #493 • FILL MY CUP LORD • 11.8.9.10}
{lyricist: Richard Blanchard}
{composer: Richard Blanchard}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 493}
{meta: tune FILL MY CUP LORD}
{meta: meter 11.8.9.10}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm]Like the woman at the [F7]well I was seeking
[Bb]For things that could not satisfy:
[F7]And then I heard my Savior speaking:
[Bb]“Draw from my well that never [Eb]shall run dry”.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Cm]Fill my [F7]cup Lord, I lift it up, [Bb]Lord!
[Bb]Come and quench this thirsting of [F7/C]my soul;
[F7/C]Bread of heaven, Feed me till I want no [Bb]more--
[Bb]Fill my cup, fill it up and make [Cm/Eb]me [Bb/D]whole!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]There are millions in this [F7]world who are craving
[Bb]The pleasures earthly [G7/B]things afford;
[F7]But none can match the wondrous treasure
[Bb]That I find in Jesus Christ [Eb]my Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]So, my brother, if the [F7]things this world gave [Bb]you
[Bb]Leave hungers that won't pass [G7/B]away,
[F7]My blessed Lord will come and save [Bb]you,
[Bb]If you kneel to Him and humbly [Eb]pray:
{end_of_verse}
